RipsMath_CalculateTicketPrize
├── it result prize number is always between 1 and n inclusive.
├── it different ticket numbers produce different prize numbers when a is odd and n is a power of two.
├── it should never revert for valid inputs.
├── when the prize number falls in the first tier
│   └── it should return the prize for that position.
├── when the prize number falls in a middle tier
│   └── it should return the prize for that position.
├── when the prize number falls in the last tier
│   └── it should return the prize for that position.
├── when the tier has a single prize
│   └── it should return the min prize.
└── when the tier has multiple prizes
    ├── when the rank is first in the tier
    │   └── it should return the min prize.
    ├── when the rank is last in the tier
    │   └── it should return the max prize.
    └── when the rank is in the middle of the tier
        └── it should linearly interpolate between min and max prize.
